---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { BUSINESS, SITE } from '../consts';

// Terms of Service. Required by the 10DLC campaign compliance checklist
// ("TOS and privacy policy are added to my website") and linked from the
// footer alongside the privacy policy.
//
// The section that matters most is "The AI Risk Scan": the scan outputs a
// risk score and names regulatory frameworks (HIPAA, PCI-DSS, CMMC, COPPA).
// Without an explicit statement that it is informational and not legal,
// compliance, or professional advice, that output is real exposure.
const EFFECTIVE = 'August 18, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms of Service"
  description="The terms that apply to using the AITS website, the AI Risk Scan, and AITS services."
  path="/terms"
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="section-label">Legal</span>
      <h1 class="section-heading">Terms of Service</h1>
      <p class="section-sub">
        Effective {EFFECTIVE}. Plain-language terms for using this site and working with us.
      </p>

      <div class="prose policy">
        <p>
          These Terms govern your use of <a href="https://aits.llc">aits.llc</a>, the AI Risk Scan,
          and any services provided by <strong>{SITE.legalEntity}</strong> ("AITS," "we," "us"). By
          using the site or our services, you agree to them. If you do not agree, please do not use
          the site.
        </p>

        <h2>Who may use this site</h2>
        <p>
          This site is intended for businesses and for people aged 16 or older. By using it you
          confirm you have the authority to act for the business you are inquiring about.
        </p>

        <h2 id="scan">The AI Risk Scan</h2>
        <div class="callout callout-strong">
          <strong>The AI Risk Scan is informational, not professional advice.</strong> It produces
          an automated score and observations based entirely on answers you supply. It is
          <strong>not</strong> legal advice, compliance certification, a security audit, an
          accounting opinion, or a substitute for a qualified professional.
        </div>
        <p>
          The scan may reference regulatory frameworks such as HIPAA, PCI-DSS, CMMC, CJIS, or
          COPPA. Those references are general context to help you decide what to look into — they
          are not a determination of whether your business complies with any law or standard, and
          they must not be relied on as one. Only a qualified attorney, auditor, or compliance
          professional can assess your obligations.
        </p>
        <p>
          Results depend on the accuracy of what you enter. Part of the report is generated with
          automated tools, including AI, which can be incomplete or wrong. Do not make legal,
          financial, or security decisions on the report alone.
        </p>

        <h2>Services, quotes and fees</h2>
        <p>
          Prices shown on this site are starting points, not offers or quotes. Actual scope and
          price are set in a written proposal or service agreement. If those documents conflict with
          this page, the signed agreement controls.
        </p>
        <p>
          Monthly services are month-to-month unless agreed otherwise. Third-party costs — software
          subscriptions, telecom and messaging fees, domain registration, advertising spend, payment
          processing — are separate from our fees unless a written agreement says they are included.
        </p>

        <h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>Provide accurate information and timely access to systems we need.</li>
          <li>Hold the rights to any content, brand assets, or data you give us to use.</li>
          <li>Maintain ownership of your own domains, payment accounts, and business records.</li>
          <li>Use anything we build lawfully, including messaging and marketing laws.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>Messaging and communications</h2>
        <p>
          If you give us your phone number and check the SMS consent box, you agree to receive text
          messages as described at the point of consent and in our
          <a href="/privacy#sms">Privacy Policy</a>. Consent is never a condition of any purchase.
          Reply STOP to opt out or HELP for help. Message and data rates may apply.
        </p>

        <h2>Intellectual property</h2>
        <p>
          The site, its content, and the AITS name and marks belong to us. Work product we create
          specifically for you transfers as set out in your service agreement. We keep ownership of
          our own methods, templates, configurations, and reusable components, and may continue to
          use general knowledge and experience gained while working with you.
        </p>

        <h2>Third-party services</h2>
        <p>
          Our work often connects to services we do not control — hosting, payment processors,
          messaging carriers, calendars, and other platforms. We are not responsible for their
          outages, policy changes, pricing, rate limits, account suspensions, or defects. Where a
          third party requires you to accept its own terms, those terms apply between you and them.
        </p>

        <h2>Disclaimers</h2>
        <p>
          The site and the scan are provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any
          kind, express or implied, including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
          non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted or error-free, or
          that any result described on this site will be achieved for your business.
        </p>

        <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the fullest extent permitted by law, AITS is not liable for indirect, incidental,
          special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost profits, revenue, data, or
          business opportunity, arising from your use of this site or the scan. Our total liability
          relating to the site or the scan will not exceed one hundred dollars ($100). Liability
          arising from paid services is governed by the applicable service agreement.
        </p>
        <p>
          Some jurisdictions do not allow certain limitations, so parts of this section may not
          apply to you.
        </p>

        <h2>Indemnification</h2>
        <p>
          You agree to indemnify and hold AITS harmless from claims arising out of information you
          provide, content or data you ask us to use, your use of anything we build, or your
          violation of these Terms or applicable law.
        </p>

        <h2>Termination</h2>
        <p>
          We may suspend or end access to the site or the scan at any time, including for misuse.
          Termination of paid services is governed by your service agreement.
        </p>

        <h2>Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These Terms are governed by the laws of the State of California, without regard to its
          conflict-of-laws rules. Any dispute relating to the site or the scan will be brought in
          the state or federal courts located in San Diego County, California, and you consent to
          that venue.
        </p>

        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these Terms. Changes take effect when posted, and the effective date above
          will be revised. Continued use of the site after a change means you accept the updated
          Terms.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>{SITE.legalEntity}</strong><br />
          {BUSINESS.street}<br />
          {BUSINESS.city}, {BUSINESS.region} {BUSINESS.postalCode}<br />
          Email: <a href={`mailto:${BUSINESS.email}`}>{BUSINESS.email}</a><br />
          Phone: <a href={`tel:${BUSINESS.phone}`}>{BUSINESS.phoneDisplay}</a>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .policy {
    color: var(--text2);
  }
  .policy h2 {
    font-family: var(--fran);
    font-size: clamp(19px, 2.2vw, 25px);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--text);
    margin: 40px 0 12px;
  }
  .policy p {
    margin-bottom: 16px;
    line-height: 1.8;
  }
  .policy ul {
    margin: 0 0 16px 20px;
  }
  .policy li {
    margin-bottom: 8px;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .policy strong {
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .callout {
    background: rgba(59, 110, 240, 0.06);
    border: 0.5px solid rgba(59, 110, 240, 0.28);
    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);
    border-radius: 0 12px 12px 0;
    padding: 20px 24px;
    margin: 24px 0;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }
  .callout-strong {
    background: rgba(0, 201, 167, 0.05);
    border-color: rgba(0, 201, 167, 0.3);
    border-left-color: var(--teal);
  }
</style>
